      "writtenOn": "2025-09-09T16:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, the EC is still supspended, but it is in the process of waking up. The ISH happens to be awake earlier, doesn\u0027t it?\nWhat happen if the EC goes to suspend, but the ISH is still up and send a message: the ISH will end up retrying CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_DSP_CLIENT_TX_RETRY_MAX times before giving up (150ms by default). Is it acceptable?\n\nShould power state transition be synchronized between ISH and EC via interrupt and acknowledgment messages?",
      "revId": "1be874cacc446ac6473429d1f47144b61e8de420",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "561f8f6f_f4f7c419",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/dsp_client_transport.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-09T22:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While AP is in suspend state, ISH power state could be any of D0/D0i0/D0i1/D0i2; this is decided by when the next scheduled task happens. So motion sense task wakes ISH to D0 and detect tablet mode change, ISH write to i2c bus to notify EC.\nMeantime, EC enables deep sleep since AP is suspended, how long EC stays in deep sleep is decided by next event time too (like hook tick every 250ms). if the i2c write arrives when EC is in deep sleep, then EC won\u0027t respond and ISH get a NACK and has to retry.\nIdeally ISH should have a way to wake up EC, probably hardware change will be required.",
      "parentUuid": "b7a107a5_3ae98b5f",
      "revId": "1be874cacc446ac6473429d1f47144b61e8de420",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c977c970_19dee484",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/dsp_client_transport.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T19:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@gwendal@chromium.org you\u0027re right, ideally we would have an interrupt from the ISH to wake the EC. We would fire it before each I2C transaction. But Uldrenite doesn\u0027t have that pin and we can\u0027t add it at this point. So the retry is the best option we have. I\u0027m looking at the EC side I2C driver to see if we can get it to handle I2C events in deep sleep and wake up when they come in instead of NACKing them.",
      "parentUuid": "561f8f6f_f4f7c419",
      "revId": "1be874cacc446ac6473429d1f47144b61e8de420",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
